## Check the implementation

Test the spoken sequence, stacked mobile layout and a view without colour. Add a new heading after the lists so later content is not mistaken for another instruction.

Use the [civica accessibility checks](../accessibility/testing.html) and compare the rendered result in light and dark modes, Vivid and Muted tones, and at 320 CSS pixels. The example markup is a starting point; a theme alone does not add its application logic.

## Source and related guidance

[NHS do and do not lists](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system/components/do-and-dont-lists) informs the component choice and interaction guidance. The examples use shared GOV.UK primitives or original civica markup, Arial typography and civica assets. NHS logos and service identity are not used.

See also [status and notifications](status.html).

## Example artwork record

The affected example records include creator, original source, rights, purpose, intended background and alternative-text decisions. Functional SVG strokes and schematic boundaries remain separate from the flat explanatory illustration style. No official identity artwork is copied.
